uTerm minimum contrast for GhosttyKit (libghostty-spm patch 0022)

Drop this file into libghostty-spm's Patches/ghostty/ (after 0021); build.sh
applies it with `git apply` on every target. It is cut against the tree with
0001-0021 applied (generic.zig is also touched by 0015), Ghostty 042b16b6.

What it does (matches vendor/SwiftTerm .../MinimumContrast.swift and
UTERM-PATCHES.md §1):
  - shaders.metal contrasted_color: hue-preserving OKLCH lightness search
    toward the WCAG target, direction by background luminance, opposite
    direction as fallback, chroma capped by the original and the sRGB gamut.
    Colors are taken from Ghostty's linear Display P3 back to linear sRGB and
    converted again afterwards.
  - shaders.metal cell_text_vertex: the NO_MIN_CONTRAST exemption for graphics
    elements (box drawing, blocks, Powerline) is ignored.
  - generic.zig: with minimum-contrast > 1 the "covering glyph" swap (U+2588
    gets its own fg as cell background) is off, so a full block is clamped
    against the real background instead of against itself.

Use with `minimum-contrast = 3` in the surface config. Measurements:
docs/ghostty-eval/measure-build-consistency.md (M13).

